        "title": "refactor(ui): deduplicate layout, clipboard, and polling scaffolds",
        "body": "Closes #105950\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI maintained duplicate dock-panel persistence, clipboard writes, polling lifecycle code, and workspace byte formatting. Those copies could drift; several copy actions already bypassed the canonical non-secure-context fallback.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds one parameterized dock-layout helper and one Lit reactive polling controller, routes all identified clipboard writes through the existing helper, and delegates workspace sizes to the shared normalization formatter. The nodes polling variant fit the controller cleanly; the non-Lit logbook state controller remains unchanged.\n\nOut of scope: duration/relative-time helpers with distinct i18n namespaces remain a follow-up product decision. The dead-export baseline remains owned by its separate burn-down task.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo visual or interaction layout changes. Copy actions now consistently retain the existing HTTP fallback; panel dimensions, polling cadence, and workspace size labels retain their prior behavior.\n\nProduction TypeScript is net 58 lines smaller. Commits are separated by dedup cluster.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBlacksmith Testboxes `tbx_01kxcrgr5m3f4ehtrkegjyv364`, `tbx_01kxcvfzkpddsbdg3w7kpc0gcq`, `tbx_01kxcw8nc7a8x4mqey2t7sgnq8`, and current-base `tbx_01kxcwt1y47whzr77vhjsbcscg`:\n\n- `pnpm test:ui`: patch-identical head passed 3,742/3,742. Rebased exact head passed 3,741/3,742; the one untouched `chat-tool-cards` DOM-query failure passed 36/36 on immediate isolated rerun.\n- Focused UI and normalization tests: 329 passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:ui` and `pnpm tsgo:core:test`: passed.\n- Full source lint plus touched-file lint: zero product findings; targeted rerun passed after one test-only cleanup.\n- Focused Chromium mock smoke: 7/7 passed, including non-secure clipboard fallback, terminal, logs, usage, and build-info flows.\n- Full Chromium mock suite: 154/158 passed. The same four failures reproduce unchanged at base `b43e832fcc8000ed7287c7accc54e381db607f85` (48/52 on both trees).\n- `oxfmt --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Dead-export check: passed with the existing baseline unchanged.\n- Fresh final-head autoreview: no findings, patch correct at 0.90 confidence.\n- The eight smaller large files lower `scripts/ts-max-loc-baseline-v2.json`. This PR passed the LOC ratchet against base `6ef3e87583eda04fc3c790b68af86e021e68733c`; current `main` at `8a2da4b1bf1555fe0bfaf705eb57300c673c81be` is independently LOC-red on seven unrelated core/Codex files.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
